            <ArticleTitle>[Genetic analysis of two pediatric patients with Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>831-834</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3760/cma.j.issn.1003-9406.2017.06.010</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To explore the genetic cause for two children with omphalocele.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The patients were examined, and the medical history of their families was collected. Methylation-specific multiplex ligation-dependent probe amplification (MS-MLPA) was performed to detect potential mutation in the patients.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Loss of methylation of imprinting center 2 (IC2) at the 11p15.5 region of the maternal chromosome was detected in both children.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The two patients were diagnosed with Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome by MS-MLPA. The loss of methylation of IC2 probably underlies the disease in both patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
